text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph again.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A copy of a graph has the same generation as the original until either is mutated. Views and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"adaptors (a transposed view, an undirected view, a wrapper such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"report their base’s generation, so a view and its base, though they may describe different","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graphs, have equal generations. ","type":"text"},{"code":"isCurrent(for:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" answers only whether the storage of the graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"passed in is in the state the generation was read from; it does not tell which view the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"generation was read through. An untracked generation, from a representation that does not track","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"generations or a mutable graph never mutated, is current for no graph. Equal tracked","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"generations are the same structural state of the same storage, and every untracked generation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"equals every other.","type":"text"}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration\/isCurrent(for:)-1rsfw","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration\/isCurrent(for:)-1t817","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration\/isCurrent(for:)-3zt2o","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration\/isCurrent(for:)-5kltt","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration\/isCurre